<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via three-day system RPs Monday.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via three-day system RPs Monday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system Monday via a round of three-day system repurchase agreements, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York confirmed.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-5/16 percent, slightly above the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate, and the same as prior to the operation.</p>
<p>(( -- John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury desk 212-859-1663))</p>
